3. **Merging Sorted Lists**: We can use a two-pointer technique to merge the lists. Initialize two pointers, one at the beginning of each list. Compare the elements at the current positions of the pointers, and add the smaller one to the merged list. Move the pointer of the smaller element forward. Repeat this process until one of the lists is exhausted. Then, append the remaining elements of the other list to the merged list.

4. **Finding the kth Element**: Once the lists are merged, the kth smallest element is simply the element at index k-1 in the merged list (since indexing starts at 0).

