B_n = B_0 * B_{n-1} + B_1 * B_{n-2} + ... + B_{n-1} * B_0

This is because each tree can be split into two subtrees, and the number of ways to form these subtrees is the product of the number of ways to form each subtree. The base cases are B_0 = 1 (an empty tree) and B_1 = 1 (a single node).

